From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: IvyCZE <me@ivy.yt>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 18:56:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Embermine: 0007-wavy-progress-lines

Draw the page-load line as a LinearWavyProgressIndicator overlay inside the
8 dp band at the edge of the address bar, so the toolbar layout does not
change. The wave is tinted with the switch-aware accent gradient (two-tone
palette when on, Firefox gradient when off) and is hidden at 0 and 100
percent. Downloads rows use a wavy bar whose amplitude drops to zero while
paused. History delete, delete browsing data and payment methods use an
indeterminate wavy bar in the accent color instead of the blue, pink and
orange progress_gradient drawable. Add JVM tests for the page-load
visibility rule and the paused amplitude.

Co-authored-by: factory-droid[bot] <138933559+factory-droid[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>

